     "t": "code",
     "text": "   ==============================================================================================\n   Matrix Type     Defining Property  Eigenvalues         Orthogonality of E.V.   Diagonalization\n   ==============================================================================================\n   Symmetric       A = A^T            Real                Orthogonal in real      Always diag. over R\n   Hermitian       A = A^theta        Real                Orthogonal in complex   Always diag. over C\n   Skew-Symmetric  A^T = -A           Purely imag. or 0   Orthogonal in complex   Always diag. over C\n   Skew-Hermitian  A^theta = -A       Purely imag. or 0   Orthogonal in complex   Always diag. over C\n   Orthogonal      A^T A = I          |lambda| = 1        Orthogonal in complex   Always diag. over C\n   Unitary         A^theta A = I      |lambda| = 1        Orthogonal in complex   Always diag. over C\n   Involutory      A^2 = I            +/- 1               Not guaranteed          Always diag.\n   Idempotent      A^2 = A            0, 1                Not guaranteed          Always diag.\n   Nilpotent       A^k = 0            0 only              Not guaranteed          NOT diag. (except 0)\n   =============================================================================================="
