     "t": "code",
     "text": "[START: Given Square Matrix A of order n]\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba Check Trace and Determinant:\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba tr(A) = sum(\u03bb_i) = sum(a_ii)\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba det(A) = prod(\u03bb_i). If det(A) = 0 \u2500\u2500\u25ba At least one \u03bb = 0 (Singular).\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba Is A Real Symmetric (A^T = A) or Hermitian (A^H = A)?\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba YES: \u2500\u2500\u25ba ALL \u03bb_i are STRICTLY REAL.\n  \u2502                 \u2500\u2500\u25ba Eigenvectors for distinct \u03bb are MUTUALLY ORTHOGONAL.\n  \u2502                 \u2500\u2500\u25ba GUARANTEED DIAGONALIZABLE (Orthogonally: P^T A P = D). STOP!\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba Is A Skew-Symmetric (A^T = -A)?\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba YES: \u2500\u2500\u25ba ALL \u03bb_i are PURE IMAGINARY (\u00b1j\u03c9) or ZERO.\n  \u2502                 \u2500\u2500\u25ba If n is ODD: det(A) = 0 and at least one \u03bb = 0 strictly.\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba Compute Characteristic Equation: det(A - \u03bb I) = 0.\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Are ALL n eigenvalues DISTINCT?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba YES: GUARANTEED DIAGONALIZABLE! (P\u207b\u00b9 A P = D). STOP!\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Are there REPEATED eigenvalues (AM(\u03bb) > 1 for some \u03bb)?\n  \u2502           \u2502\n  \u2502           \u251c\u2500\u25ba For each repeated \u03bb, compute Geometric Multiplicity:\n  \u2502           \u2502     GM(\u03bb) = n - rank(A - \u03bb I)\n  \u2502           \u2502\n  \u2502           \u251c\u2500\u25ba Does GM(\u03bb) = AM(\u03bb) for ALL eigenvalues?\n  \u2502           \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba YES: DIAGONALIZABLE! (Full set of n independent eigenvectors).\n  \u2502           \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba NO (GM < AM): DEFECTIVE MATRIX! (Cannot be diagonalized)."
