     "text": "[START: Given Quadratic Form Q(X) = X^T A X (A is Real Symmetric)]\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba Step 1: Inspect Diagonal Entries a_ii:\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Are there mixed signs (e.g. a\u2081\u2081 > 0 and a\u2082\u2082 < 0)?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba YES: AUTOMATICALLY INDEFINITE! STOP!\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Is ANY a_ii \u2264 0 while testing for Positive Definite?\n  \u2502           \u2514\u2500\u25ba YES: CANNOT BE POSITIVE DEFINITE. Continue to test ND/Indefinite.\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba Step 2: Evaluate Sylvester's Leading Principal Minors \u0394_k:\n  \u2502     \u2502   \u0394\u2081 = a\u2081\u2081,  \u0394\u2082 = |a\u2081\u2081 a\u2081\u2082; a\u2082\u2081 a\u2082\u2082|,  \u0394\u2083 = det(A).\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Are ALL \u0394_k > 0 (\u0394\u2081 > 0, \u0394\u2082 > 0, \u0394\u2083 > 0, ...)?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba YES: POSITIVE DEFINITE (PD)! (All \u03bb_i > 0). STOP!\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Do signs strictly alternate starting negative: \u0394\u2081 < 0, \u0394\u2082 > 0, \u0394\u2083 < 0, ...?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba YES: NEGATIVE DEFINITE (ND)! (All \u03bb_i < 0). STOP!\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Does it violate both PD and ND patterns (e.g. \u0394\u2081 > 0, \u0394\u2082 < 0)?\n  \u2502           \u2514\u2500\u25ba If det(A) \u2260 0: INDEFINITE! (Mixed eigenvalue signs). STOP!\n  \u2502\n  \u2514\u2500\u25ba Step 3: If det(A) = 0 (At least one \u03bb = 0):\n        \u251c\u2500\u25ba Find eigenvalues \u03bb_i directly:\n        \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba All \u03bb_i \u2265 0 (with at least one 0): POSITIVE SEMI-DEFINITE (PSD).\n        \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba All \u03bb_i \u2264 0 (with at least one 0): NEGATIVE SEMI-DEFINITE (NSD).\n        \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Mixed signs: INDEFINITE."
